WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.034
-I hate to ask this,

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.903
but what animals did you bring
for us tonight?

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.571
-It's exciting.
We've got El Jefe.

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:07.773
We've got Mishka.
There's some pretty cool ones.

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.976
-Yeah. I always think, the cuter
the name, the scarier the thing.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.310
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.614
-Well, first of all, I've got
a pretty interesting one.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:18.251
Now, this is actually right back
here. This is a millipede.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.154
Now, its name is
Millie Bobby Brown.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.722
Because millipede.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.258
And she actually recently
visited us at the zoo.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.660
But what you want to do --
Put your hand out.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.861
-Oh, no.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.796
-And we'll actually use
kind of like a bracelet.

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:32.065
-No.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.766
-Now, this is actually
a giant African millipede.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:37.303
And they'll wrap around,
naturally, around your wrist.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.706
Now, the cool thing
with millipedes

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.541
is they have about 400 legs.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:44.444
And when they get --
when they get stressed.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.378
-Oh, my gosh!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.378 --> 00:00:48.013
Oh, my gosh. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:48.013 --> 00:00:52.185
-Now, they don't bite.
They release an acidic smell.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.020
It's like a terrible foul smell.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.555
That's how they evade predators.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.490
So you've got nothing
to worry about.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.125
-Yeah, until I go out for dinner
after the show, yeah.

00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:02.862
-It's amazing, yeah. But they've
got all those segments.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.863
And these guys
are one of the first animals

00:01:04.863 --> 00:01:06.766
to ever colonize land.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.368
They have a very important part
in our history.

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.003
So, really fascinating animals.

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:13.039
They feel like
a little toothbrush.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.007
Don't you think?

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.741
-That really is totally bizarre.

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:17.777
-Look, he's saying hi.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.178
He's like, "Hi, everyone."

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:21.747
-That's so interesting
because I'm saying bye.

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:23.949
That's so, so interesting.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:25.384
-All right, that was good.

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:26.418
How cute is that?

00:01:26.418 --> 00:01:28.054
-Oh, my God, that was so gross.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.122
Oh, my gosh. Gosh!

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.256
-That was great.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.325
-What was his name?
Did he have a name?

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.826
-This is Millie Bobby Brown.

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.662
-The cuter the name,
the scarier the animal.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.029
Okay, good.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:39.599
-For this next one, we are going
to go down onto the floor.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.668
-Okay, let's go.
-I'm going to grab some milk.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:42.802
[ Audience aws ]

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:45.571
Here we go. So...

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:46.772
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:48.942
-This little guy here,
this is little Sebastian.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.277
He's a little miniature horse.
[ Applause ]

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.545
Sebastian.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.580
You're welcome to hold
that bottle if you'd like.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.516
-Sure.
-He loves his milk,

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.651
just like from the show
"Parks and Recreation."

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.087
-That's how you named him?
-Little Sebastian.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.121
-Little Sebastian.

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:04.223
-And he is a miniature horse,

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.626
probably the most adorable
animal on the face of the Earth.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:08.361
-Oh, my goodness.
-He's just incredible.

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.896
-Just beautiful.

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:12.431
-Now, the thing with these guys

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.200
is they're actually
really important animals

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.969
because they act as
service animals.

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:20.907
So often you'll see them as
therapy animals or guide animals

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.676
helping people around,
and they're really interesting.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.145
You know, they don't get
above 38 inches.

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:30.283
That's the highest one would
ever get -- is 38 inches tall.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:33.019
Really, really small,
but they are just so cute.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.754
I'll tell you another thing
that they like.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.022
When he's done with his milk,

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.691
you can get your face right up
close to his nose.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.993
And if you just lightly blow
on his nose,

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:43.196
that's like a form of greeting
for him.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:45.264
So you're welcome
to give that a go.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.466
Just so he recognizes you.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:49.802
Look over there.
Do you want to see Jimmy?

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:50.569
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:51.871
There you go.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.073
So he gave you a little kiss.
-He gave me a kiss.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.509
-There you go. Good job.
[ Applause ]

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.544
-Thank you, little Sebastian.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:02:59.712
-Good boy.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.680
-We love you, little Sebastian.
Come back.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.549
-All right, we'll see you later,
buddy.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.251
-You'll always be little
Sebastian.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.285
-Okay, there we go.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:07.853
-Robert, this is great.
Fantastic.

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:09.055
Thank you very, very much.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.490
I love him. Thank you.
-Bye.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.224
-Oh, come back, please.
We love you.

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:14.493
-Oh, that's great.
[ Applause ]

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:16.362
That's awesome.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.964
-All right.
We're down to our final?

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.266
-This is our final animal.
-Okay.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.667
-I need a little bit of warning
for you --

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:25.338
just follow my movement and
don't make any sudden movements.

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.438
[ Audience ohs ]

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:27.840
Really nice and slow.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.375
Hey, how's it going? Hi.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.876
This is a mandrill.

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:34.747
Now, mandrills, they're one of
my favorite primates.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:35.982
Here you go.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:39.118
Now, this little mandrill,
Mishka --

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.752
Hey, Mishka.

00:03:40.752 --> 00:03:42.822
She loves her plush toys.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:46.892
She's just like any other young
animal who loves her toys,

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:49.395
and they really need that
for enrichment.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:54.167
They really need to move around
a lot to experience new things.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:57.136
And what we'll do, if we get
some of her favorite toys out,

00:03:57.136 --> 00:04:00.072
she might be able to come over
here and say hi.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:01.274
What do you think, Mishka?

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.409
-This is beautiful. Wow.
-Now, the mandrill --

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.110
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.379
The mandrill is really
interesting.

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:09.715
See, what they do
is they actually --

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:12.084
Oh, he's got some food.
She's hungry.

00:04:12.084 --> 00:04:13.519
Now, what the mandrills do

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.988
is they actually have that
really brightly colored bottom,

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.957
and that's how they signal
to each other.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.925
You can see she's using
her hands there.

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:21.260
You're all right, little one.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.662
And she is incredible.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.998
The largest of the old-world
monkeys.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.699
Beautiful bright coloration.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:30.937
The males will get this
incredible vibrant red color.

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.505
Oh, she likes her seal.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:35.541
Now, although these animals
are really nice and cute,

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.243
